      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخيّف أَلْوَانًا</span></b>  <i>He</i> (a man, TA) <i>altered so as
to become of different colours.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخيّفت الإِبِلُ</span> <i>The camels took different directions</i>
in the place of pasturage (Lh, JK) &amp;c. (Lh.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخيّفهُ</span> <i>He took by little and little from it;</i>
(IAar, JK;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تخوّفهُ</span> [q. v.]. (JK.)

